# What never reaches the build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the one that bites. The obvious one is size: a
# venv or an htmlcov directory in the context is megabytes uploaded to the
# daemon on every build for nothing. The other is cache invalidation: the
# Dockerfile's `COPY app/` is the layer that changes on every commit, and
# anything swept into the context that changes more often than the source does
# would invalidate layers that had no reason to rebuild.
#
# Nothing here is a substitute for the Dockerfile copying only what it needs.
# The build copies `requirements-lambda.txt` and `app/` and nothing else, so
# tests and development dependencies stay out of the image whatever this file
# says. This is the belt to that file's braces.

# Version control and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/.DS_Store

# Python build and cache artifacts
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
.env
.env.*

# Test and coverage output
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
tests/

# The development dependency set. `requirements-lambda.txt` is the runtime pin
# set and the only one the Dockerfile installs; this one carries pytest, moto,
# black, mypy, locust and curl_cffi, none of which belong in a Lambda image.
# Excluded so a stray `COPY . .` in a future edit cannot pick it up either.
requirements.txt

# Local development scaffolding and one-off operational scripts, none of which
# belongs in a Lambda image. `scripts/` holds table creation, backfills and the
# perf gate; all of them are run by a software engineer against an environment,
# never by a function.
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
scripts/
README.md

# Tool configuration, used by the test and lint jobs rather than at runtime.
pytest.ini
mypy.ini
pyproject.toml
pyrightconfig.json
runtime.txt
.bandit

# Seed data for the category and manufacturer tables. Read by
# `scripts/` at seed time against a table, never by a request path, so it is
# context weight and image weight for nothing.
static_assets/

# Editor state
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
